arm: dts: rockchip: rk356x: always prefer SD card over eMMC for FIT loading

board_boot_order() (arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl-boot-order.c) builds the
SPL boot-device search list by walking u-boot,spl-boot-order in source
order and stops at the first device that yields a valid FIT. The
"same-as-spl" keyword resolves to whichever device the BootROM itself
already used to load idbloader.img/SPL (board_spl_was_booted_from()),
and is inserted at the front of that list.

On this SoC family the BootROM's own device probing (independent of
U-Boot, fixed in mask ROM) is not something this property can
influence. When the BootROM happens to boot SPL from eMMC in a given
power-on cycle (e.g. no SD card present at that moment, a transient
SD init failure, etc.) and eMMC also carries a valid u-boot.itb,
"same-as-spl" causes SPL to try and succeed on eMMC first - the
explicit &sdmmc0 entry later in the list is never reached in that
boot, even though it is listed ahead of &sdhci.

Dropping "same-as-spl" makes the FIT search order unconditionally
SD-first, eMMC-second, regardless of which device the BootROM used to
load SPL itself. bootph-pre-ram/bootph-some-ram for the sdmmc0
controller and its pinctrl groups, as well as for sdhci, are already
set earlier in this file and need no changes. The SD card's power
rail (vcc3v3_sd, on the RK809 PMIC) is regulator-always-on and
regulator-boot-on in the board dts, matching how sdhci's own supply
is handled here (no bootph tag on the PMIC/i2c chain either) - so no
additional bootph tagging is needed for the regulator.

--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk356x-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk356x-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
 	};
 
 	chosen {
-		u-boot,spl-boot-order = "same-as-spl", &sdmmc0, &sdhci;
+		u-boot,spl-boot-order = &sdmmc0, &sdhci;
 	};
 
 	dmc: dmc {
